.TH "CSDLC-GITHUB-PR" "1" "September 11, 2026" "C-SDLC v3" "ADL Operator Manual"
.SH NAME
csdlc\-github\-pr \- create, update, ready or merge a reviewed PR
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&csdlc github\-pr \-\-request REQUEST [\-\-observe\-github] [\-\-execute]
\&csdlc github\-pr \-\-help
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\&With \-\-execute owns pull_request_create, pull_request_update, pull_request_ready and pull_request_merge. Only this command owns merge. Merge requires explicit authorization naming the repository and numeric PR, matching independent exact\-head review, merge method, base and authenticated policy/check admission. Unsupported policy and uncertain outcomes fail closed.
.SH OPTIONS
\&\-\-request: Required path to a UTF\-8 JSON request of the command's request family.
.PP
\&\-\-observe\-github: Perform authenticated GitHub readback. Requires selected credentials. It does not itself create, update or merge a PR.
.PP
\&\-\-execute: Select typed operational dispatch, not a generic force flag. Cannot combine with \-\-observe\-github on non\-pr\-state remote routes.
.PP
\&\-\-help: Show standalone help; \-h is equivalent.
.PP
\&\-h: Show standalone help; do not combine with execution options.
.SH REQUEST
\&Without \-\-execute: RemoteRouteRequest, including typed review/readback receipt references when required. With \-\-execute on non\-pr\-state: OperationalRemoteDispatchRequest, whose expected_lifecycle_digest is the canonical authority selector payload digest, not the local issue index digest. See csdlc\-requests(1).
.PP
\&Non\-pr\-state \-\-execute plus \-\-observe\-github is rejected. \-\-observe\-github without \-\-execute uses authenticated readback in the planning path; it does not turn the returned plan into a performed mutation. Request family must match the selected mode.
.SH EFFECTS
\&Readback/planning does not perform remote mutation. Operational github mutation writes durable intent before network dispatch and retains authenticated reconciliation/receipt. Successful review/publish plan reports are not PR creation. Credential names are scoped to the adapter; no raw token in argv or request.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
\&csdlc github\-pr \-\-request pr\-create\-dispatch.json \-\-execute
.fi
.PP
\&Request fixtures are in docs/csdlc\-v3/man/examples/; values are illustrative and must be bound to the actual head and reviewed issue. See csdlc\-workflow(1) for the full live sequence.
.SH RECOVERY
\&After uncertain dispatch retain the original request and exact intent. Reinvoke the identical native request for authenticated reconciliation. A changed request is a different operation, not a retry. Never delete the target guard or intent to force a second write.
.PP
\&Issue\-edit does not support write replay, including retry_after_authenticated_absence; reconcile exact retained target and preserve later human changes. Supported create/ready absence retry is explicit, authenticated and one\-shot. Merge retries are always read\-only; a still\-open or uncertain PR remains blocked.
.SH SEE ALSO
\&csdlc(1), csdlc\-requests(1), csdlc\-workflow(1), csdlc\-finish(1).
.SH MERGE
\&mutation.action pull_request_merge requires base, method \(dqmerge\(dq, review_receipt_path and review_receipt_digest. Squash/rebase, queues, unsupported active rules, incomplete pagination, missing/wrong\-app checks, skipped required checks, unresolved threads and changes\-requested reviews fail closed.
.PP
\&Admission observes exact PR/head/base and effective branch policy. The SHA conditional protects the head, not an atomic base/policy snapshot. Reconciliation requires the authenticated merge commit to have two ordered parents, matching retained base then reviewed head. A base race after dispatch can only be detected afterward; never claim atomic policy compare\-and\-swap or automatic rollback.
.PP
\&After successful merge reconciliation run finish \-\-observe\-github independently. A merge receipt is not terminal issue\-close evidence.
.SH MERGE LINKAGE
\&Merge requires reviewed publication_linkage, one canonical whole\-line Closes owner/repository#issue or Part of owner/repository#issue relation, complete authenticated closingIssuesReferences and a qualified OPEN issue before dispatch. Same\-repository #issue is supported; split\-repository references must be qualified. Closing poststate requires CLOSED, PartOf requires OPEN. Head CAS does not freeze body, base or policy; late drift blocks reconciliation and never authorizes another PUT. See docs/csdlc\-v3/PULL_REQUEST_MERGE.md.
